@startuml
' diagrams/failover-flow.puml
title System Failover — Database Primary Loss (maps to Chaos Experiment CE-001)

participant "Monitoring /\nHealth Checks" as MON
database "DB Shard N\n(PRIMARY)" as PRIMARY #FFCCCC
participant "Patroni\n(HA Manager)" as PATRONI
database "DB Shard N\n(REPLICA — most\ncaught-up WAL)" as REPLICA
participant "PgBouncer" as PGB
participant "Account Svc" as ACC
participant "Transaction\nOrchestrator" as ORCH
queue "Kafka" as KAFKA

PRIMARY -x PRIMARY: **crash / becomes unresponsive**
MON -> PRIMARY: health check
PRIMARY --> MON: **no response** (missed heartbeats)

note over MON, PATRONI
  Detection window: configured health-check
  interval + failure threshold, targeting
  well under the 30s single-component RTO.
end note

MON -> PATRONI: primary unhealthy, initiate failover
PATRONI -> REPLICA: check WAL position\n(select most caught-up replica)
PATRONI -> REPLICA: **promote to PRIMARY**
REPLICA -> REPLICA: replay any remaining WAL,\naccept new writes

note over PATRONI #FFCCCC
  **Fencing:** old primary (if it recovers) is
  fenced via a monotonically increasing epoch/
  fencing token, preventing a split-brain where
  both nodes accept writes simultaneously
  (mitigates FM-004: network partition / split-brain).
end note

PATRONI -> PGB: update routing config\n(new primary endpoint)
PGB -> PGB: reload connection pool,\ndrain connections to old primary

par in-flight requests during the gap
  ACC -> PRIMARY: UPDATE accounts ... (in flight at crash time)
  PRIMARY --> ACC: **connection failure**
  ACC -> ACC: CB-DB-PRIMARY trips\n(2 failures / 5s threshold)
  note over ACC
    Fallback per reference table:
    "Route reads to replica; queue writes"
    Writes are queued (bounded queue, timeout-
    bound) rather than immediately failed, to
    absorb the failover window gracefully.
  end note
end

PGB -> REPLICA: new connections routed here\n(now acting as primary)
ACC -> REPLICA: retry queued writes
REPLICA --> ACC: success

ORCH -> ORCH: periodic sweep (10s interval)\nfinds any sagas mid-flight on shard N\nat crash time
alt saga step had not committed
  ORCH -> ORCH: resume saga (retry step against new primary)
else saga step had partially committed elsewhere
  ORCH -> ORCH: trigger compensation\n(per Failure Scenario 2 logic)
end

ACC -> ACC: CB-DB-PRIMARY: HALF_OPEN,\nprobe succeeds, CLOSED
KAFKA -->> KAFKA: **unaffected** — separate failure\ndomain, other shards' events\ncontinue processing normally

note over MON, ORCH
  **Success criteria (ties to CE-001):**
  Zero committed transaction loss;
  p99 < 5s during the failover window;
  full recovery within 30s RTO.
end note

@enduml